              highlighted: ["AB","EL"] },
            { text: "Again, apply {EI}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB}, to {EF} producing {EN} as breadth.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EI","AD","DB","EN"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "I",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "N",    name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "MGIN", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "But the square on {AB} also equals {EL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","EL"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder, twice the rectangle {AD} by {DB}, equals {HI}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AD","DB","HI"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AD² + DB² = 2 AD·DB + AB²", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is medial and equals {EG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB","EG"] },
            { text: "therefore {EG} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {EM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","EF","EM"] },
            { text: "therefore {EM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EM rational, incommensurable in length with EF", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Again, since twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is medial and equals {HG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB","HG"] },
            { text: "therefore {HG} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HG"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {HM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HG","EF","HM"] },
            { text: "therefore {HM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["HM","EF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "HM rational, incommensurable in length with EF", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "therefore {EG} is also incommensurable with {HG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EG","HG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {EM} is also incommensurable in length with {MH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","HM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EG : HG = EM : MH", ref: "VI.1" },
                               { claim: "EM, MH incommensurable in length", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {EM} and {MH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","HM"] },
            { text: "Therefore {EH} is an apotome, and {HM} an annex to it.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "EH an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that {EH} is again an apotome and {HN} an annex to it.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HN"] },
            { text: "Therefore to an apotome different rational straight lines are annexed",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EH","HM","HN"] },
            { text: "which are commensurable with the wholes in square only, which was proved impossible.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["EM","EN"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "only one annex to an apotome", ref: "X.79" }] },
            { text: "Therefore no other straight line can be so annexed to {AB}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "Therefore to {AB} only one straight line can be annexed which is incommensurable in square with the whole",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CB","AC"] },
            { text: "and which with the whole makes the squares on them added together medial,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "twice the rectangle contained by them medial,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"] },
            { text: "and also the sum of the squares on them incommensurable with twice the rectangle contained by them.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AC","CB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.84") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7": "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "VI.1": "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "X.11": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.22": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.73": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.78": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX78/",
        "X.79": "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX79/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Set out a rational straight line {EF}. Apply {EG}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB}, to {EF} producing {EM} as breadth. Apply {HG}, equal to twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, to {EF} producing {HM} as breadth. Then the remainder, the square on {AB}, equals {EL}. Therefore {AB} is the side of {EL}. [!just II.7]

Again, apply {EI}, equal to the sum of the squares on {AD} and {DB}, to {EF} producing {EN} as breadth.

But the square on {AB} also equals {EL}, therefore the remainder, twice the rectangle {AD} by {DB}, equals {HI}. [!just II.7]

Now, since the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is medial and equals {EG}, therefore {EG} is also medial. And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {EM} as breadth, therefore {EM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}. [!just X.22]

Again, since twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB} is medial and equals {HG}, therefore {HG} is also medial. And it is applied to the rational straight line {EF} producing {HM} as breadth, therefore {HM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {EF}. [!just X.22]

Since the sum of the squares on {AC} and {CB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AC} by {CB}, therefore {EG} is also incommensurable with {HG}. Therefore {EM} is also incommensurable in length with {MH}. [!just VI.1; X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {EM} and {MH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {EH} is an apotome, and {HM} an annex to it. [!just X.73]

Similarly we can prove that {EH} is again an apotome and {HN} an annex to it. Therefore to an apotome different rational straight lines are annexed which are commensurable with the wholes in square only, which was proved impossible. [!just X.79]

Therefore no other straight line can be so annexed to {AB}. Therefore to {AB} only one straight line can be annexed which is incommensurable in square with the whole and which with the whole makes the squares on them added together medial, twice the rectangle contained by them medial, and also the sum of the squares on them incommensurable with twice the rectangle contained by them.

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
